e wasn't a Christian believer. Then he went he heard people praying in the church. Then he was impressed. Then he went to his father.", "He told him stay on religion for your forefathers. Then he asked him what is the source of this religion? They told him it's in Levant. So then he was waiting for travelers and uh then he tried to find people in Levant. Then he found this bishop and then he saw that this bishop in the church is a liar. Basically he tells people something and he asked them for money and he keeps the money to himself and he said when that bishop died essentially another person of uh took his place. We have another bishop now. Then he saw that he praised him for his good character, good manners and all of that.", "So he went to him to learn from him and he asked him about his beliefs. So that bishop said to Al Far and this is very important keep that in mind that bishop said far that I do not know anyone today who is on the same beliefs that I'm upon today. So he told him people have perished changed and abandoned most of what they were upon. So he's talking about people changing true religion of what the Christianity should have been at that time following Jesus which should have been they've changed the alter. perish. They abandoned what that which they should have been upon except for one man.", "So now we're talking about the people who had remnants of truth of what that gospel was near the time of the prophet wasam. They were very very few. Very very few were actually having this the true beliefs and like I said these were remnants of the scriptures remnants of the Torah and the gospel. He said to him except uh one person a man in Mosul. So Sal Pharisee went to him and then he he informed him about another person and then in the end a bishop told him I don't want to know anyone else that is on the same faith as us.", "So whatever we believe now as a group at that time he's definitely not talking about Christians because there was like millions of